    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15588" root="رشد" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَرَاشِدُ</span></b> , a pl. without a sing., like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحَاسِنُ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلَامِحُ</span>, (L,) <i>The right places to which roads
tend;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَقَاصِدُ الطُّرُقِ</span>. (S, L, K.) You say,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ يَهْدِى إِلَى المَرَاشِدِ</span> [<i>He directs to the right
places to which roads tend</i>]. (A.)

